Enhancement: Record memory usage during a run

A backup that the kernel's OOM killer stops leaves no error behind to explain
itself, because `SIGKILL` cannot be caught. Setting `RESTIC_DIAG_LOG` to a file
now makes restic record, as it runs, how much memory it is using — its own heap
figures alongside what the cgroup reports, which is what the kernel decides on.
Each line is flushed as it is written, so the last one says what restic was using
when it was killed. `RESTIC_DIAG_INTERVAL` sets how often to sample, 10 seconds
by default.

